# Input
```js
/* should generate diagnostics */
2 ^ 32;
3 ^ 3;
10 ^ 6;
0 ^ 0;
2 ^ 8;
2  ^  8;
const x = 2 ^ 8;
foo(2 ^ 8);
10 ^ 1_000;
2 ^ 8 ^ 2;
2 /* comment */ ^ 8;
2 ^ /* comment */ 8;
2 ^
	8;
(2) ^ (8);

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.js:2:3 lint/nursery/noXorAsExponentiation  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! This bitwise XOR operator ^ is used between two integer literals.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ 2 ^ 32;
      │   ^
    3 │ 3 ^ 3;
    4 │ 10 ^ 6;
  
  i In JavaScript, ^ is the bitwise XOR operator, not exponentiation. The exponentiation operator is **.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Unsafe fix: Replace ^ with **.
  
     1  1 │   /* should generate diagnostics */
     2    │ - 2·^·32;
        2 │ + 2·**·32;
     3  3 │   3 ^ 3;
     4  4 │   10 ^ 6;
  

```

